  "id": "DrugBank_DB06215 - MONDO_1356",
  "verbalization": "Ferumoxytol is associated with Iron Deficiency Anemia through a series of indirect pathways, primarily via the indication of Microcytic Anemia and Ferric Oxide. The evidence suggests that Ferumoxytol may act as a mediator in the pathogenesis of Iron Deficiency Anemia, potentially by influencing the production or utilization of iron in the body. The presence of Ferric Oxide as an indication for Iron Deficiency Anemia indicates that Ferumoxytol may contribute to the development of this condition by affecting iron metabolism. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the shared pathway through Ferric Oxide and Microcytic Anemia suggests a possible role in the pathophysiology of Iron Deficiency Anemia. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ferumoxytol to influence iron-related processes, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism.",
